# Example Claude Desktop Configuration

## Configuration Location

**macOS**: `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`

**Windows**: `%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json`

## Basic Configuration

Point Claude Desktop to use the claude-byom proxy:

```json
{
  "environmentVariables": {
    "ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL": "http://127.0.0.1:3000",
    "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY": "any-value-works"
  }
}
```

## Important Notes

1. The `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` can be any value - it's not used by the proxy
2. The `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` should point to where your claude-byom proxy is running
3. Make sure the proxy server is running before starting Claude Desktop
4. Restart Claude Desktop completely after changing the configuration

## Different Port

If you're running the proxy on a different port:

```json
{
  "environmentVariables": {
    "ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL": "http://127.0.0.1:3001",
    "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY": "any-value-works"
  }
}
```

## Using localhost instead of 127.0.0.1

Some systems prefer localhost:

```json
{
  "environmentVariables": {
    "ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL": "http://localhost:3000",
    "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY": "any-value-works"
  }
}
```

## Complete Example with MCP Servers

If you also have MCP servers configured, combine them:

```json
{
  "environmentVariables": {
    "ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL": "http://127.0.0.1:3000",
    "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY": "any-value-works"
  },
  "mcpServers": {
    "filesystem": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem", "/path/to/workspace"]
    }
  }
}
```
